<section class="content">
<div class="introbox"><h2>How to use this atlas</h2><p>Har topic ko simple definition → intuition/example → evidence/equations → open questions/limitations ke order mein samjho. Difficult topics ko prerequisites ke baad kholo. Sirf terms yaad karna goal nahi hai; concepts ke beech connections samajhna goal hai.</p></div>
<div id="master" class="divider"><span>01</span><h2>MASTER KNOWLEDGE ROADMAP</h2></div>
<article class="knowledge-card" id="master-0">
          <div class="card-head"><span class="section-no">START</span><h3>Introduction &amp; Study Framework</h3><span class="chevron">⌄</span></div>
          <div class="card-body"><p>THE KNOWLEDGE MULTIVERSE</p><p>Master Roadmap — Science, Philosophy, Mind, Society, Technology &amp; Beyond</p><p>Purpose: Yeh PDF ek encyclopedia nahi hai. Yeh ek connected knowledge map hai: har heading tumhe batati hai ki</p><p>kya padhna hai, aur short explanation batata hai ki concept ka core kya hai.</p><p>Study rule: Har topic ko 4 steps mein padho — (1) simple definition, (2) example/intuition, (3) evidence/equations,</p><p>(4) open questions &amp; limitations.</p><h4>MASTER INDEX</h4><p>#      Field                                                                             Topics</p><p>1      HOW TO LEARN &amp; THINK                                                              10</p><p>2      MATHEMATICS UNIVERSE                                                              15</p><p>3      CLASSICAL PHYSICS                                                                 17</p><p>4      RELATIVITY &amp; SPACETIME                                                            10</p><p>5      QUANTUM UNIVERSE                                                                  36</p><p>6      ASTRONOMY &amp; COSMOLOGY                                                             19</p><p>7      CHEMISTRY                                                                         14</p><p>8      BIOLOGY, EVOLUTION &amp; GENETICS                                                     19</p><p>9      EARTH, CLIMATE &amp; ENVIRONMENT                                                      14</p><p>10     NEUROSCIENCE, MIND &amp; CONSCIOUSNESS                                                17</p><p>11     CORE PHILOSOPHY                                                                   16</p><p>12     WESTERN PHILOSOPHY                                                                24</p><p>13     INDIAN PHILOSOPHY                                                                 13</p><p>14     BUDDHIST &amp; JAIN PHILOSOPHY                                                        14</p><p>15     ISLAMIC, PERSIAN &amp; SUFI THOUGHT                                                   13</p><p>16     CHINESE &amp; JAPANESE PHILOSOPHY                                                     10</p><p>17     SOCIAL &amp; POLITICAL PHILOSOPHY                                                     11</p><p>18     ECONOMICS &amp; FINANCE                                                               15</p><p>19     COMPUTER SCIENCE &amp; INFORMATION                                                    19</p><p>20     ENGINEERING &amp; TECHNOLOGY                                                          13</p><p>21     HISTORY &amp; CIVILIZATIONS                                                           18</p><p>22     LANGUAGE, LITERATURE &amp; ARTS                                                       17</p><p>23     PSYCHOLOGY &amp; HUMAN BEHAVIOUR                                                      10</p><p>24     MEDICINE &amp; HEALTH LITERACY                                                        11</p><p>25     LAW, GOVERNMENT &amp; CIVICS                                                          9</p><p>26     FRONTIERS &amp; DEEP QUESTIONS                                                        15</p><p>Knowledge Multiverse — Master Roadmap                                                                             Page 1</p><p>HOW TO BECOME GENUINELY KNOWLEDGEABLE</p><p>Knowledge ka matlab sirf terms yaad karna nahi. Ek knowledgeable person kisi idea ko simple words mein explain kar</p><p>sakta hai, evidence aur uncertainty ko identify karta hai, aur us idea ko doosre fields se connect kar sakta hai.</p><p>Foundation order: Scientific method -&gt; mathematics -&gt; classical physics -&gt; chemistry -&gt; biology -&gt; computing -&gt;</p><p>psychology/neuroscience -&gt; philosophy.</p><p>Deep order: Relativity -&gt; quantum mechanics -&gt; cosmology -&gt; quantum information -&gt; consciousness -&gt;</p><p>metaphysics -&gt; comparative philosophy -&gt; frontier research.</p><p>Golden habit: Jab bhi koi impressive claim suno, 5 questions poochho: “Evidence kya hai?”, “Alternative</p><p>explanation?”, “Kitni uncertainty?”, “Kis sense mein true?”, “Kya isko test kiya ja sakta hai?”</p><p>STATUS LABELS</p><p>Established = strong evidence and broad scientific/philosophical acceptance. Active research = evidence hai but</p><p>major questions open hain. Speculative = interesting proposal/hypothesis, not established fact.</p><p>Knowledge Multiverse — Master Roadmap                                                                         Page 2</p></div>
        </article>
<article class="knowledge-card" id="master-1">
          <div class="card-head"><span class="section-no">01</span><h3>HOW TO LEARN &amp; THINK</h3><span class="chevron">⌄</span></div>
          <div class="card-body"><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">1</span>Scientific Method</div><p>Observation -&gt; question -&gt; hypothesis -&gt; test -&gt; data -&gt; conclusion -&gt; replication.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">2</span>Correlation vs Causation</div><p>Do cheezein saath badal rahi hain to zaroori nahi ki ek doosri ko cause kare.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">3</span>Falsifiability</div><p>Aisa possible test hona chahiye jo claim ko galat dikha sake.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">4</span>Bayesian Thinking</div><p>Evidence aane par belief ko probability ke saath update karna.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">5</span>Critical Thinking</div><p>Claim, evidence, assumptions, alternatives aur uncertainty ko alag-alag check karo.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">6</span>Cognitive Biases</div><p>Confirmation bias, anchoring, availability, sunk cost aur framing jaise systematic thinking errors.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">7</span>Information Literacy</div><p>Textbook, review paper, primary study, news aur social-media claim ke evidence levels samjho.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">8</span>Logic &amp; Arguments</div><p>Premise -&gt; inference -&gt; conclusion; valid reasoning aur true premises dono important hain.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">9</span>Probability</div><p>Chance, conditional probability, expected value aur risk.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">10</span>Statistics</div><p>Mean, variance, distributions, sampling, regression aur uncertainty.</p></div><h4>SELF-TEST</h4><ul><li>Is section ka sabse basic question kya hai?</li><li>Iske 3 concepts ko ek doosre se connect karke samjhao.</li><li>Is field mein kya established hai aur kya abhi uncertain/open hai?</li></ul><p>Knowledge Multiverse — Master Roadmap                                                                 Page 3</p></div>
        </article>
<article class="knowledge-card" id="master-2">
          <div class="card-head"><span class="section-no">02</span><h3>MATHEMATICS UNIVERSE</h3><span class="chevron">⌄</span></div>
          <div class="card-body"><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">1</span>Arithmetic</div><p>Numbers, fractions, ratios, percentages, powers, roots aur scientific notation.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">2</span>Algebra</div><p>Variables, equations, inequalities, polynomials aur functions.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">3</span>Geometry</div><p>Angles, triangles, circles, coordinates aur transformations.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">4</span>Trigonometry</div><p>sin, cos, tan; triangles, rotations aur waves.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">5</span>Vectors</div><p>Magnitude + direction; velocity, force aur fields mein essential.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">6</span>Calculus</div><p>Derivative = change ki rate; integral = accumulation/area.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">7</span>Limits</div><p>Kisi quantity ke kisi value ke bahut paas jaane par behaviour.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">8</span>Differential Equations</div><p>Unknown function aur derivatives wali equations; motion, growth aur fields mein.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">9</span>Linear Algebra</div><p>Vectors, matrices, eigenvalues/eigenvectors; quantum mechanics aur AI mein.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">10</span>Complex Numbers</div><p>Real + imaginary numbers; waves, circuits aur quantum theory mein.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">11</span>Probability &amp; Statistics</div><p>Random variables, distributions, expectation aur inference.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">12</span>Discrete Mathematics</div><p>Sets, logic, graphs, counting aur algorithms.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">13</span>Number Theory</div><p>Prime numbers, divisibility aur modular arithmetic; cryptography ka base.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">14</span>Topology</div><p>Continuous stretching ke under shape ki properties; modern math aur physics mein.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">15</span>Mathematical Logic</div><p>Formal proof, consistency, completeness aur formal systems.</p></div><h4>SELF-TEST</h4><ul><li>Is section ka sabse basic question kya hai?</li><li>Iske 3 concepts ko ek doosre se connect karke samjhao.</li><li>Is field mein kya established hai aur kya abhi uncertain/open hai?</li></ul><p>Knowledge Multiverse — Master Roadmap                                               Page 4</p></div>
        </article>
<article class="knowledge-card" id="master-3">
          <div class="card-head"><span class="section-no">03</span><h3>CLASSICAL PHYSICS</h3><span class="chevron">⌄</span></div>
          <div class="card-body"><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">1</span>Units &amp; Dimensions</div><p>SI units, dimensional analysis aur physical quantities.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">2</span>Kinematics</div><p>Position, velocity, acceleration aur motion ka description.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">3</span>Newton&#x27;s Laws</div><p>Inertia, F=ma aur action-reaction; classical mechanics ka backbone.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">4</span>Work, Energy &amp; Power</div><p>Force se energy transfer, kinetic/potential energy aur power.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">5</span>Momentum &amp; Collisions</div><p>Momentum conservation, impulse aur elastic/inelastic collisions.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">6</span>Rotational Mechanics</div><p>Torque, angular momentum, moment of inertia aur rolling.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">7</span>Gravitation</div><p>Newtonian gravity, orbits, escape velocity aur Kepler laws.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">8</span>Oscillations</div><p>Simple harmonic motion, resonance aur damping.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">9</span>Waves</div><p>Frequency, wavelength, phase, interference aur standing waves.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">10</span>Fluid Mechanics</div><p>Pressure, buoyancy, viscosity aur flow.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">11</span>Thermodynamics</div><p>Temperature, heat, work, internal energy aur laws of thermodynamics.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">12</span>Statistical Mechanics</div><p>Microscopic particles se temperature, pressure aur entropy ka connection.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">13</span>Electrostatics</div><p>Charge, Coulomb law, electric field aur potential.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">14</span>Circuits</div><p>Current, voltage, resistance aur Kirchhoff laws.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">15</span>Magnetism</div><p>Magnetic fields, Lorentz force aur magnetic materials.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">16</span>Electromagnetic Induction</div><p>Changing magnetic flux se EMF; generators aur transformers.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">17</span>Maxwell&#x27;s Equations</div><p>Electricity aur magnetism ko unified electromagnetic theory mein jodti hain.</p></div><h4>SELF-TEST</h4><ul><li>Is section ka sabse basic question kya hai?</li><li>Iske 3 concepts ko ek doosre se connect karke samjhao.</li><li>Is field mein kya established hai aur kya abhi uncertain/open hai?</li></ul><p>Knowledge Multiverse — Master Roadmap                                          Page 5</p></div>
        </article>
<article class="knowledge-card" id="master-4">
          <div class="card-head"><span class="section-no">04</span><h3>RELATIVITY &amp; SPACETIME</h3><span class="chevron">⌄</span></div>
          <div class="card-body"><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">1</span>Special Relativity</div><p>High-speed motion mein time, length aur simultaneity observer ke frame par depend kar sakte hain.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">2</span>Lorentz Transformations</div><p>Different inertial observers ke space-time coordinates ko relate karti hain.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">3</span>Time Dilation</div><p>Different frames mein elapsed time different measure ho sakta hai.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">4</span>Length Contraction</div><p>Motion ki direction mein measured length frame-dependent hoti hai.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">5</span>Relativistic Energy</div><p>E=mc^2 aur full energy-momentum relation.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">6</span>Equivalence Principle</div><p>Locally gravity aur acceleration ke effects ko equivalent treat kiya ja sakta hai.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">7</span>General Relativity</div><p>Gravity ko spacetime geometry/curvature ke framework mein describe karti hai.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">8</span>Geodesics</div><p>Curved spacetime mein free-falling bodies ke natural paths.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">9</span>Gravitational Time Dilation</div><p>Strong gravity mein clocks differently tick karte hain.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">10</span>Gravitational Waves</div><p>Massive accelerating systems se spacetime mein propagating ripples.</p></div><h4>SELF-TEST</h4><ul><li>Is section ka sabse basic question kya hai?</li><li>Iske 3 concepts ko ek doosre se connect karke samjhao.</li><li>Is field mein kya established hai aur kya abhi uncertain/open hai?</li></ul><p>Knowledge Multiverse — Master Roadmap                                                               Page 6</p></div>
        </article>
<article class="knowledge-card" id="master-5">
          <div class="card-head"><span class="section-no">05</span><h3>QUANTUM UNIVERSE</h3><span class="chevron">⌄</span></div>
          <div class="card-body"><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">1</span>Crisis of Classical Physics</div><p>Blackbody radiation, photoelectric effect aur atomic spectra ne classical models ki limits dikhayi.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">2</span>Planck</div><p>Energy quantisation ka early idea.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">3</span>Einstein &amp; Photons</div><p>Photoelectric effect ko light quanta se explain kiya.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">4</span>Bohr Model</div><p>Hydrogen ke quantised energy levels ka early atomic model.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">5</span>de Broglie</div><p>Matter particles ke saath wave nature associate ki.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">6</span>Heisenberg</div><p>Matrix mechanics aur uncertainty principle ke major architect.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">7</span>Schrodinger</div><p>Wave mechanics aur Schrodinger equation.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">8</span>Born Rule</div><p>Wavefunction ki probability interpretation.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">9</span>Dirac</div><p>Relativistic quantum theory aur antimatter prediction mein major contribution.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">10</span>Wave-Particle Duality</div><p>Quantum objects ko simple classical particle/wave categories mein fit nahi kiya ja sakta.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">11</span>Superposition</div><p>Quantum state multiple basis states ke combination mein ho sakti hai.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">12</span>Wavefunction</div><p>Quantum state ko mathematically represent karne wali object.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">13</span>Uncertainty Principle</div><p>Position aur momentum jaise pairs ko arbitrarily precise simultaneously nahi kiya ja sakta.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">14</span>Quantum Tunnelling</div><p>Classically forbidden region ke across non-zero quantum probability.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">15</span>Entanglement</div><p>Composite quantum states mein unusually strong correlations.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">16</span>EPR</div><p>Quantum completeness aur nonlocal correlations par foundational argument.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">17</span>Bell&#x27;s Theorem</div><p>Local hidden-variable theories aur quantum predictions ke beech experimentally testable difference.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">18</span>Measurement Problem</div><p>Quantum evolution aur definite measurement outcomes ko reconcile karne ka puzzle.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">19</span>Copenhagen Interpretation</div><p>Measurement-centered interpretation family.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">20</span>Many-Worlds</div><p>Knowledge Multiverse — Master Roadmap                                                                 Page 7</p></div><p>Wavefunction collapse ke bina quantum theory ko interpret karne ka proposal.</p><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">21</span>Decoherence</div><p>Environment interactions quantum interference ko effectively suppress kar sakte hain.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">22</span>Spin</div><p>Intrinsic quantum angular momentum; classical spinning ball ka literal version nahi.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">23</span>Quantum Statistics</div><p>Bosons/fermions aur Bose-Einstein/Fermi-Dirac statistics.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">24</span>Quantum Field Theory</div><p>Particles ko quantum fields ke excitations ke roop mein describe karti hai.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">25</span>QED</div><p>Quantum electrodynamics: charged matter + electromagnetic field.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">26</span>QCD</div><p>Quantum chromodynamics: quarks + gluons + strong interaction.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">27</span>Standard Model</div><p>Elementary particles aur strong/weak/electromagnetic interactions ka framework; gravity included nahi.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">28</span>Quantum Information</div><p>Qubit, measurement, entanglement, channels aur information.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">29</span>Quantum Computing</div><p>Quantum states se computation; selected problems mein potential speedups.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">30</span>Quantum Gravity</div><p>Quantum theory aur gravity ko consistent framework mein combine karne ki research.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">31</span>String Theory</div><p>Fundamental entities ko one-dimensional strings ke models.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">32</span>M-Theory</div><p>Different string theories ko broader higher-dimensional framework mein relate karne ka proposal.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">33</span>Extra Dimensions</div><p>Four-dimensional spacetime ke beyond dimensions ke theoretical models.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">34</span>Loop Quantum Gravity</div><p>Spacetime geometry ko quantum degrees of freedom se quantise karne ka approach.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">35</span>Holographic Principle</div><p>Gravitational systems mein bulk physics ko lower-dimensional boundary description se relate karne ka idea.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">36</span>AdS/CFT</div><p>Gravity in AdS space aur lower-dimensional conformal field theory ke beech duality.</p></div><h4>SELF-TEST</h4><ul><li>Is section ka sabse basic question kya hai?</li><li>Iske 3 concepts ko ek doosre se connect karke samjhao.</li><li>Is field mein kya established hai aur kya abhi uncertain/open hai?</li></ul><p>Knowledge Multiverse — Master Roadmap                                                                        Page 8</p></div>
