          <div class="card-body"><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">1</span>Prehistory</div><p>Archaeology, early humans, tools, migration aur agriculture.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">2</span>Mesopotamia</div><p>Early cities, writing, states aur law.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">3</span>Ancient Egypt</div><p>Pharaonic civilization, writing, religion aur engineering.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">4</span>Indus Valley Civilization</div><p>Urban planning, trade, crafts aur undeciphered script.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">5</span>Ancient China</div><p>Dynasties, bureaucracy, philosophy aur technology.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">6</span>Ancient Greece</div><p>City-states, philosophy, democracy, science aur art.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">7</span>Roman World</div><p>Republic, empire, law, engineering aur Mediterranean networks.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">8</span>Indian Civilizations</div><p>State formation, literature, mathematics, science aur diverse traditions.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">9</span>Islamic Golden Age</div><p>Mathematics, astronomy, medicine, philosophy aur translation.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">10</span>Medieval Europe</div><p>Feudal institutions, religion, cities, trade aur intellectual life.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">11</span>Renaissance</div><p>Art, humanism, science aur changing institutions.</p></div><div class="topic"><div class="topic-name"><span class="topic-num">12</span>Scientific Revolution</div><p>Mathematical and experimental approaches